From: satyanandh-ai <satyanandh-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:51:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Two-stage retrieval: rank by snippet, refine top candidates
 with full job descriptions

Short search-result snippets can undersell (or oversell) a posting -
years-of-experience and specific tech stacks often only appear in the
full description, not the 2-line preview. Retrieval now works in two
bounded stages:

- retrieval.py: stage 1 ranks all postings by snippet (as before, no
  extra network calls). Stage 2 fetches the FULL description (via
  Wire's in_job_details) for only the top candidates, concurrently
  (bounded worker pool), with a tight per-call timeout and an overall
  stage timeout - a slow/failed fetch just leaves that posting on its
  snippet rather than blocking the search. Disabled by default unless
  a country_domain is passed, so existing callers are unaffected.
- wire_client.py: search_jobs now also returns the resolved country
  code (needed to route detail fetches). get_job_details exposes
  max_wait_seconds/max_retries/retry_delay so bulk enrichment can use
  a tighter budget than a one-off lookup would.
- analyzer.py: the LLM now reads the full description (up to 3000
  chars) when available, instead of a 500-char snippet, and is told
  explicitly which postings have full text vs a short preview.
- app.py: threads the resolved country through, surfaces enrichment
  progress in the status widget, and flags in the raw-data view which
  postings' ranking used a full description.

NOTE: the exact field name Wire's in_job_details uses for the full
description text is unconfirmed (no live API access to verify) -
_fetch_full_description checks several plausible keys defensively.
Needs a real run to confirm which one Wire actually returns.
